## 🎯 Quality Checklist (Before Commit)

- [ ] All tests pass: `pytest tests/`
- [ ] No linting errors: `ruff check .`
- [ ] Code formatted: `ruff format --check .`
- [ ] Type checking passes: `mypy app`
- [ ] Coverage ≥80%: `pytest --cov=app --cov-fail-under=80`
- [ ] Docstrings added for new functions
- [ ] Commit message follows convention
- [ ] No `TODO` or `FIXME` comments (create issues instead)
- [ ] File sizes within limits (200 lines source, 300 lines tests)

### Test Execution (MANDATORY)

**✅ GOOD: Always run tests with visible output/logging**
```bash
# Always use -v (verbose) or tee to capture output
pytest tests/ -v 2>&1 | tee /tmp/test_results.log
pytest tests/unit/ --tb=short -v
pytest tests/ --tb=no -q 2>&1 | tail -50  # Show summary at end
```

**❌ BAD: Running tests silently without logs**
```bash
pytest tests/  # No output - cannot diagnose failures
pytest tests/ > /dev/null  # Discards output
```

**Key Requirements:**
- **ALWAYS** use `-v` (verbose) or `-q` (quiet summary) - never silent
- **ALWAYS** use `tee` to save output when running long test suites
- **ALWAYS** show progress/logs - user needs to see what's happening
- Use `--tb=short` for faster output, `--tb=no` for summary only
- Use `tail -N` to show last N lines of output for summary

